From 8998c2ec6f249b058e80f07f2da2fd00d069a9f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wayne <wayne@localhost>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 03:08:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add a service-account computer API for external agent
 harnesses

A program outside Rakazo can now obtain and drive a computer without ever receiving the sandbox supervisor URL or token: the surface is gated by a service bearer plus a bot identity, and every call is re-authorized against the operator-configured space, so a caller cannot widen its reach by naming someone else's computer.

Routes cover the full lifecycle an external harness needs: provision, exec, file read/write, observe, browser, stop, and destroy. Disabled entirely unless both the token and the space are configured.
